WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.180 --> 00:00:00.810
MARK MIRCHANDANI:
The public sector

00:00:00.810 --> 00:00:03.090
has a big responsibility,
and that requires

00:00:03.090 --> 00:00:04.710
using the right technology.

00:00:04.710 --> 00:00:07.080
Join us in historic
downtown Austin, Texas,

00:00:07.080 --> 00:00:09.690
as we talk to SoftServe about
how the public sector has

00:00:09.690 --> 00:00:12.180
been adopting the cloud
with Google Cloud Partners.

00:00:12.180 --> 00:00:14.465
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:15.755 --> 00:00:17.130
Thanks for joining
us today, Ron.

00:00:17.130 --> 00:00:18.900
Can you tell us a little
more about SoftServe?

00:00:18.900 --> 00:00:20.317
RONALD ESPINOSA:
Sure, absolutely.

00:00:20.317 --> 00:00:25.050
SoftServe is a curious company,
starting about 26 years ago,

00:00:25.050 --> 00:00:27.870
founded by some rocket
scientists and their PhD

00:00:27.870 --> 00:00:32.970
students, set out to solve
problems in the data world,

00:00:32.970 --> 00:00:35.563
complex software
issues, and systems

00:00:35.563 --> 00:00:37.230
that just didn't want
to talk and didn't

00:00:37.230 --> 00:00:38.760
want to play together.

00:00:38.760 --> 00:00:42.360
The company is now
pushing 10,000 people,

00:00:42.360 --> 00:00:45.102
spread around close
to 30 delivery centers

00:00:45.102 --> 00:00:45.810
across the globe.

00:00:45.810 --> 00:00:48.840
MARK MIRCHANDANI: So SoftServe
is a Google Cloud Partner.

00:00:48.840 --> 00:00:50.520
What does that mean
for companies who

00:00:50.520 --> 00:00:51.823
choose to work with SoftServe?

00:00:51.823 --> 00:00:52.740
RONALD ESPINOSA: Sure.

00:00:52.740 --> 00:00:53.907
Well, it means a few things.

00:00:53.907 --> 00:00:57.150
It means that we have
best-in-breed technologies

00:00:57.150 --> 00:00:58.110
to work with.

00:00:58.110 --> 00:01:01.200
It means that we've got
several certified people

00:01:01.200 --> 00:01:02.400
on Google Cloud.

00:01:02.400 --> 00:01:05.370
It means that we work
hand in glove with GCP

00:01:05.370 --> 00:01:07.110
to be certain that
our clients are

00:01:07.110 --> 00:01:11.310
getting the best of both
worlds, not just technology

00:01:11.310 --> 00:01:14.910
for technology's sake, but
technology for people's sake,

00:01:14.910 --> 00:01:17.610
and making sure that
those pieces of technology

00:01:17.610 --> 00:01:20.310
are delivered in concert
with the end goal,

00:01:20.310 --> 00:01:22.380
and that end goal is
determined in concert.

00:01:22.380 --> 00:01:24.860
MARK MIRCHANDANI: How does this
look for the public sector?

00:01:24.860 --> 00:01:26.527
RONALD ESPINOSA: Well,
the public sector

00:01:26.527 --> 00:01:28.350
is its own animal,
as we all know.

00:01:28.350 --> 00:01:31.200
They have a very
big responsibility.

00:01:31.200 --> 00:01:33.760
And the responsibility is
to the lives of the people,

00:01:33.760 --> 00:01:34.770
their constituents.

00:01:34.770 --> 00:01:36.330
What happens on the roadways?

00:01:36.330 --> 00:01:37.660
What happens in the buildings?

00:01:37.660 --> 00:01:39.930
What happens in the communities?

00:01:39.930 --> 00:01:43.560
And when they look into
technology solutions,

00:01:43.560 --> 00:01:46.480
they tend to be limited
because of that lens.

00:01:46.480 --> 00:01:48.720
So bringing in somebody
like an outside partner,

00:01:48.720 --> 00:01:51.000
like a SoftServe, to
work with technologies

00:01:51.000 --> 00:01:53.790
that municipalities know they
need or the public sector

00:01:53.790 --> 00:01:56.280
in general knows they need,
or suspects they may need

00:01:56.280 --> 00:01:58.590
sometimes, it puts
them in a position

00:01:58.590 --> 00:02:00.180
of really being
able to stay focused

00:02:00.180 --> 00:02:02.790
on what their mission
is, while outsourcing

00:02:02.790 --> 00:02:05.770
to us to be able to come in and
give them really expert advice.

00:02:05.770 --> 00:02:08.020
MARK MIRCHANDANI: That's a
really great way to put it.

00:02:08.020 --> 00:02:11.640
And one of those examples for
technologies is the cloud.

00:02:11.640 --> 00:02:13.290
What does that look
like for SoftServe

00:02:13.290 --> 00:02:15.270
to partner with these
public sector entities

00:02:15.270 --> 00:02:17.160
and then look at implementing
things in the cloud?

00:02:17.160 --> 00:02:18.077
RONALD ESPINOSA: Sure.

00:02:18.077 --> 00:02:19.800
So there is the
initial reticence,

00:02:19.800 --> 00:02:21.900
the challenges that go with--

00:02:21.900 --> 00:02:24.330
it's not mine, it's
not in my four walls,

00:02:24.330 --> 00:02:26.460
I don't have a team of
people to manage it.

00:02:26.460 --> 00:02:28.860
But shortly behind that
comes the realization

00:02:28.860 --> 00:02:31.770
that you really don't
have control over this.

00:02:31.770 --> 00:02:34.278
There are employees who are
using their own devices,

00:02:34.278 --> 00:02:35.820
that are accessing
personal accounts,

00:02:35.820 --> 00:02:38.170
and are doing their
shopping and whatever else.

00:02:38.170 --> 00:02:41.250
And so you do have outside
influence on your own network.

00:02:41.250 --> 00:02:43.860
But then you get into
the costs of supporting

00:02:43.860 --> 00:02:47.070
these massive server farms
that you'd need to support--

00:02:47.070 --> 00:02:50.610
connected and autonomous
vehicles, connected devices

00:02:50.610 --> 00:02:51.830
to the environment.

00:02:51.830 --> 00:02:53.850
There's the scale
that you need to be

00:02:53.850 --> 00:02:56.250
able to operate within that.

00:02:56.250 --> 00:02:59.130
And so when you start
considering these things,

00:02:59.130 --> 00:03:01.620
and you think about your
public sector responsibility

00:03:01.620 --> 00:03:04.647
to be frugal while
being responsible,

00:03:04.647 --> 00:03:06.480
it makes a lot of sense
to move to the cloud

00:03:06.480 --> 00:03:08.917
and really look into
how you can do that.

00:03:08.917 --> 00:03:10.500
One of the things
we really like to do

00:03:10.500 --> 00:03:12.510
is focus in on assessments
and making sure

00:03:12.510 --> 00:03:14.980
that those assessments
result in a plan.

00:03:14.980 --> 00:03:16.980
And Google Cloud is very
much in sync with that.

00:03:16.980 --> 00:03:18.330
MARK MIRCHANDANI: Well, thanks
so much for coming in, Ron,

00:03:18.330 --> 00:03:20.970
and telling us about how
SoftServe helps enable

00:03:20.970 --> 00:03:22.950
companies, including
the public sector,

00:03:22.950 --> 00:03:25.290
to really understand and
do more with their data.

00:03:25.290 --> 00:03:25.860
RONALD ESPINOSA: Sure.

00:03:25.860 --> 00:03:27.068
I appreciate the opportunity.

00:03:27.068 --> 00:03:28.086
Thank you.

00:03:28.086 --> 00:03:29.327
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:03:29.327 --> 00:03:30.910
MARK MIRCHANDANI:
Thanks for watching,

00:03:30.910 --> 00:03:33.035
and stay tuned as we talk
more about the technology

00:03:33.035 --> 00:03:36.670
behind building a smart
city with SoftServe.

